@startuml
' Source Use Case: UC-011 — Get Outfit Recommendations
' Primary Specification: ../use-cases/UC-011-get-outfit-recommendations.md
' Supporting Authorities: ../SRS.md (v0.3); ../business-rules.md (v0.1.2)
' Business/Product: ../../01-business/BRD.md (v0.3); ../../02-product/PRD.md (v0.2)
' Master Actors/Scope: ../use-cases/use-case-diagram.puml
' Process Authority: ../../../Initial files/CapsuleAI_Scrum_Development_Workflow.md, Sections 11, 39–42, 46
' Version: 0.1; Status: Baseline Draft
' SRS trace: FR-OUT-001, FR-OUT-003, FR-OUT-005, FR-OUT-010, FR-OUT-011, FR-OUT-012, ERR-OUT-001, ERR-OUT-002, ERR-WEATHER-001, FR-OUT-009
' Rule trace: BRULE-AUTH-001, BRULE-GAR-003, BRULE-OUT-008, BRULE-OUT-009, BRULE-OUT-006, BRULE-PERS-003, BRULE-PERS-004
' Flow coverage: UC Sections 6–10; alternatives and failures retain their textual meaning.
' The textual Use Case Specification remains the normative behavioral source.

title AD-011 - Get Outfit Recommendations
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false

|User|
start
:Request outfits; provide or accept occasion/style;
|CapsuleAI|
if (Authorized access usable?) then (Yes)
    :Identify available authorized wardrobe/context;
else (No)
    :Pause protected use; require renewed access (UC-002);
    stop
endif
repeat
    :Prepare wardrobe, preferences and relevant context/evidence;
    if (Usable current weather available?) then (Yes)
        :Use identified environmental evidence;
    else (No / stale)
        :Disclose missing environment;
        :Consume UC-006 freshness/acquisition fallback;
        note right
          Weather currentness <=30 minutes.
          Acquisition delay <=2 seconds.
          Skip only unavailable environmental filtering.
          Preserve all remaining hard validity.
        end note
    endif
    :Identify confirmed, active, owned garments
ready for applicable checks;
    if (Remaining information supports assessment?) then (Yes)
    else (Insufficient)
        :Explain missing ready roles/attributes or context;
        :Withhold a completed zero-choice claim;
        |User|
        :Revise existing inputs and request again when useful;
        stop
    endif
    |CapsuleAI|
    :Form candidate combinations from eligible owned garments;
    :Apply structural, layering, bulk, pattern
and available environmental hard validity;
    :Determine distinct valid outfit set;
    if (Evaluation/result available?) then (Yes)
    else (Unavailable)
        :Explain unavailable recommendations;
        |User|
        :Retry request or return to available wardrobe/context;
        stop
    endif
    |CapsuleAI|
    if (Relevant basis still current?) then (Yes)
    else (Changed)
        :Refresh advice or mark prior assessment Outdated;
        :Withhold current result until established;
        |User|
        :Retry current request after review/recovery;
        stop
    endif
    |CapsuleAI|
    if (Any valid outfits?) then (Yes)
        :Apply soft personalized ranking to valid outfits;
        if (At least three distinct valid outfits?) then (Yes)
            :Present at least three valid choices;
        else (One or two)
            :Present actual valid choices; explain limitation;
        endif
        :Show identities and supported reasons;
        |User|
        :Select an outfit to inspect;
        |CapsuleAI|
        :Show owned constituents, context and explanation;
        :Offer separate Shuffle, feedback and Wear actions;
        |User|
        :Choose outfit, browse or start separate supported action;
    else (Completed zero)
        |CapsuleAI|
        :Explain no valid outfit under evaluated context;
        :Offer evidence-supported input revision;
        |User|
        :Review available wardrobe/context adjustments;
    endif
    if (Request under revised occasion/context or inputs?) then (Yes)
        :Revise supported request inputs;
    endif
repeat while (Request another assessment?) is (Yes) not (No)
|CapsuleAI|
:Finish with actual valid choices or completed zero;
:Viewing alone creates no feedback, Wear or ownership;
stop

@enduml
